# These fixtures are compared BYTE FOR BYTE against what this build emits and
# accepts, so any end-of-line normalisation makes the comparison meaningless -
# and would make it fail on a checkout with core.autocrlf=true while passing on
# CI, which is the worst way for a conformance test to be wrong.
#
# -text switches conversion off in both directions, so every checkout gets the
# committed bytes rather than a CRLF rendering of them.
#
# README.md is deliberately not listed; it is an ordinary source file.
*.json -text
